#
# deploy/tests/mirror-sync: the dumps an official mirror follows — the
# full dump, the differences, the chain index and its hashes, the
# retention that follows the snapshots, and a mirror that reproduces the
# origin's tree with btrfs receive.
#
# The test needs root, btrfs-progs and loop devices, and skips itself
# (exit 77) when it cannot have them. A skip is not a pass, so this
# wrapper checks the same prerequisites first and fails with what to do
# about it — a gate that goes green because it never ran is worse than
# no gate.
set -euo pipefail

root="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
test_script="$root/deploy/tests/mirror-sync"
name="test.d/mirror-sync"

if [ ! -x "$test_script" ]; then
  echo "$name: $test_script is not there or not executable." >&2
  exit 1
fi

if [ "$(id -u)" -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "$name: needs root — it creates loop devices and mounts filesystems." >&2
  echo "Run: sudo scripts/test mirror-sync" >&2
  exit 1
fi

missing=()
for binary in mkfs.btrfs btrfs losetup mount umount findmnt flock jq; do
  command -v "$binary" >/dev/null 2>&1 || missing+=("$binary")
done
if [ "${#missing[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then
  echo "$name: missing ${missing[*]}. Install btrfs-progs, util-linux and jq first" >&2
  echo "(e.g. apt install btrfs-progs util-linux jq)." >&2
  exit 1
fi

status=0
"$test_script" "$@" || status=$?
if [ "$status" -eq 77 ]; then
  echo "$name: the test skipped itself although the prerequisites are met — see its" >&2
  echo "SKIP message above. Treated as a failure, because a skipped check proves nothing." >&2
  exit 1
fi
exit "$status"
